d_at":"2019-03-21T12:32:08Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/475227920","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/6952#issuecomment-475227920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/6952","id":475227920,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NTIyNzkyMA==","user":{"login":"aehlig","id":9567293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NjcyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9567293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig","html_url":"https://github.com/aehlig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-03-21T13:27:26Z","updated_at":"2019-03-21T13:27:26Z","body":"> @aehlig could you take a look at this crash bug? Relevant stacktrace from logs: [...]\r\n\r\nFrom the _quoted_ stack trace, the last call in the Bazel code base (`HttpConnector.java:93`) is `url.openConnection(proxy)` which itself is a legitimate way of opening a connection. For the calls further up the stack, I can only guess. However, the comment for the `javax.crypto.JceSecurityManager` class reads as follows.\r\n\r\n```\r\n/**\r\n * The JCE security manager.\r\n *\r\n * <p>The JCE security manager is responsible for determining the maximum\r\n * allowable cryptographic strength for a given applet/application, for a given\r\n * algorithm, by consulting the configured jurisdiction policy files and\r\n * the cryptographic permissions bundled with the applet/application.\r\n *\r\n * <p>Note that this security manager is never installed, only instantiated.\r\n *\r\n * @author Jan Luehe\r\n *\r\n * @since 1.4\r\n */\r\n```\r\n\r\nFrom that I would guess that we're either getting into legal territory, or have an incompletely configured host java. Both are, however, outside the scope of Bazel. So the only thing bazel can do here, is to hide the stack trace and report a permanent error for the attempt of fetching the given repository: https://bazel-review.googlesource.com/c/bazel/+/93750","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/475227920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"aehlig","id":9567293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NjcyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9567293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig","html_url":"https://github.com/aehlig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2219697911,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MjIxOTY5NzkxMQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/eve